      "content": "Sudden sensor trips and cooling shutdowns can be caused by several things, such as a failing compressor, a sudden power surge, or a faulty sensor itself misleading the main control unit. Electrical glitches or a blown fuse in the system's control panel are also common culprits for an abrupt failure with no clear log entry. Given the perishables, focus your actions on emergency cooling and monitoring, as diagnosing the exact failure might take time.",
